---
layout: product.njk
og_type: website
breadcrumbs:
  - text: Home
    url: /
  - text: RosterWise Apps
eleventyComputed:
  title: "RosterWise™ — College Recruiting Intelligence Apps | Free to Try"
  description: "RosterWise™ apps for college {{ apps.sports | selectattr('live') | pluck('name') | andList | lower }} recruiting: roster depth, class-year gaps, recruiting pathways and My RosterFit™ fit bands for each program. Free to try; $39.99 once for full access."
  faq:
    - q: "Is RosterWise free?"
      a: "Free to try. Download the app and open three programs in full, plus one conference, and browse every program on the map and in the list before you decide. Full access is one in-app purchase of $39.99."
    - q: "Is this a subscription?"
      a: "No. Full access is a one-time purchase of $39.99: no subscription, no renewals, no ads. You pay once and keep it for your athlete's whole recruiting journey."
    - q: "Which sports and divisions does RosterWise cover?"
      a: "{{ apps.sports | coverageAnswer | safe }}"
    - q: "How current are the rosters?"
      a: "Rosters are read from each school's own athletics site, and every roster is labeled with its season. A program whose newest roster isn't complete yet keeps showing its last complete one, so a half-posted roster never stands in for the real team. New rosters arrive with app updates."
    - q: "Will I get future updates?"
      a: "Yes. Your purchase includes the app's updates for the sport you buy, and each season's new rosters arrive in them."
    - q: "Does it work on iPad?"
      a: "Yes. Each app runs on iPhone and iPad."
    - q: "Do I need an account? Where does my athlete's information go?"
      a: "No account and no login. Your athlete's My RosterFit™ profile stays on your device and in your own iCloud. It's never sent to us. <a href='/privacy/'>Read the privacy policy.</a>"
    - q: "What is My RosterFit™?"
      a: "My RosterFit™ checks how each program lines up with your athlete, factor by factor: room at your athlete's position, academics, distance and cost, plus height, roster make-up and your pathway's level in the sports that score them. Each factor gets a light, Strong, Moderate or Low, and each program gets one fit band from the lights: Strong, Good, Mixed or Weak fit. It reads your athlete's position, graduation year, test scores, home and travel distance, and budget, and height and pathway where the sport scores them. There's no single number, and programs are never ranked. It's not a guarantee of admission or a roster spot — it's a data-informed starting point for building a smarter recruiting list. <a href='/roster-intelligence/'>Learn more about our roster intelligence methodology.</a>"
    - q: "Will RosterWise tell me which schools will recruit my athlete?"
      a: "No — and we're upfront about that. No tool can predict recruiting outcomes, because they depend on individual circumstances, coach communication, timing, and many factors no dataset can capture. What RosterWise does is give families the analysis to make better-informed decisions about where to focus their recruiting effort. It's intelligence, not a crystal ball."
    - q: "Do you offer recruiting consulting or coach outreach?"
      a: "No. RosterWise is a self-service intelligence tool, not a recruiting service. We focus on giving families the data and analysis to do their own research — because nobody knows your athlete's situation better than your family."
---
{#- The apps' sales page (board app-page; Scott's marks, 2026-11-01). One sport is "chosen" at a time: the hero's
    chips, its video, the tours, the try-free button and the closing button all follow it (src/assets/app-page.js).
    Without JavaScript the first live sport shows, and every link still works. Everything per sport comes from
    apps.json (names, coverage, store links, art) and previews.json (videos, their questions, the team floors), so a
    sport that goes live, or gets its videos, appears here with no edit to this page. -#}
{% set live = apps.sports | selectattr("live") %}
{% set soon = apps.sports | rejectattr("live") %}
{% set reel = apps.sports | withPreviews(previews) %}
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/app-page.css?v=2">

{% import "app-macros.njk" as ap %}

<!-- Hero: choose a sport, see its Fit tour, one App Store badge -->
<section class="product-hero ap-hero" id="top">
  <div class="ap-hero-grid">
    <div class="ap-hero-copy">
      <p class="ap-eyebrow">RosterWise&trade; apps &middot; iPhone &amp; iPad</p>
      <h1>Find the College Programs<br>Where Your Athlete Actually Fits</h1>
      <p class="tagline">Deep roster intelligence for recruiting families, in a dedicated app for each sport.</p>

      {% if live.length > 1 %}
      <div class="ap-chips" role="group" aria-label="Choose a sport">
        {% for s in live %}
        <button type="button" class="ap-chip" data-ap-sport="{{ s.slug }}" aria-pressed="{{ 'true' if loop.first else 'false' }}">
          <img src="{{ s.logo }}" alt="" width="36" height="36" loading="eager"><span>{{ s.name }}</span>
        </button>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
      {% endif %}

      <div class="ap-cta">
        {% for s in live %}
        <div class="ap-cta-set" data-ap-for="{{ s.slug }}"{% if not loop.first %} hidden{% endif %}>
          <a class="ap-badge" href="{{ s.appStoreUrl }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            <img src="/assets/badges/download-on-the-app-store-black.svg" alt="Download RosterWise {{ s.name }} on the App Store" width="150" height="50">
          </a>
          {{ ap.rating(s, "ap-rating--hero", appRatings) }}
        </div>
        {% endfor %}
        <p class="ap-offer"><b>Free to try.</b> $39.99 once for full access. No subscription.</p>
        {% if reel.length %}<a class="ap-watch" href="#tours">&#9654;&ensp;Watch the three tours with sound</a>{% endif %}
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="ap-hero-media">
      {% for s in live %}
      {% set loopFor = true %}{% set loopHidden = not loop.first %}{% include "app-loop.njk" %}
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>

  {% if soon.length %}
  <p class="ap-soon">
    {% for s in soon %}<img src="{{ s.logo }}" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy">{% endfor %}
    <span>{{ soon | pluck("name") | andList }} {{ "are" if soon.length > 1 else "is" }} on the way.
    {% for s in soon %}{% if s.hub %}<a href="{{ s.hub }}">{{ s.name }} guides&nbsp;&rarr;</a> {% endif %}{% endfor %}</span>
  </p>
  {% endif %}
</section>

<!-- Proof: the team floors the videos and the store state, and the terms -->
<section class="ap-proof">
  <div class="ap-proof-inner">
    {% if reel.length %}
    <ul class="ap-stats">
      {% for s in reel %}{% set floor = s.slug | teamFloor(previews) %}{% if floor %}
      <li><b>{{ floor }}</b><span>college {{ s.name | lower }} teams</span></li>
      {% endif %}{% endfor %}
    </ul>
    {% endif %}
    <p class="ap-terms"><span>Rosters read from each school&rsquo;s own athletics site</span><span>No login</span><span>No ads</span><span>No subscription</span></p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- The three tours, each beside the questions it answers (previews.json) -->
{% if reel.length %}
<section class="product-section product-section--cream ap-tours" id="tours">
  <div class="container">
    {% for s in live %}
    <div class="ap-tour-set" data-ap-for="{{ s.slug }}" data-reels{% if not loop.first %} hidden{% endif %}>
      {% include "app-tours.njk" %}
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>
{% endif %}

<!-- Try it free -->
{% set tfSports = live %}{% include "app-try-free.njk" %}

<!-- One app for each sport -->
<section class="product-section product-section--white ap-sports" id="sports">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="ap-kicker">Pick your sport</p>
    <h2>One app for each sport</h2>
    <p class="ap-lead">Each app is built for its sport: its positions or weight classes, its divisions, its recruiting.</p>
    <ul class="ap-cards">
      {% for s in live %}
      <li class="ap-card">
        {% if s.storeArt %}<img class="ap-card-art" src="{{ s.storeArt }}" alt="" width="960" height="411" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
        {% else %}<div class="ap-card-art ap-card-art--plain"><img src="{{ s.logo }}" alt="" width="96" height="96" loading="lazy"></div>{% endif %}
        <div class="ap-card-body">
          <img class="ap-card-icon" src="{{ s.logo }}" alt="" width="52" height="52" loading="lazy">
          <div>
            <h3>RosterWise&trade; {{ s.name }}</h3>
            <p class="ap-card-cov">{{ s.subtext }}</p>
            {{ ap.rating(s, "ap-rating--card", appRatings) }}
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="ap-card-acts">
          <a class="ap-btn ap-btn--ink" href="{{ s.appStoreUrl }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Get the app</a>
          {% set pillSport = s %}{% include "reels-pill.njk" %}
        </div>
        {% if s.downloadPage %}<a class="ap-card-more" href="{{ s.downloadPage }}">More about RosterWise {{ s.name }}&nbsp;&rarr;</a>{% endif %}
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
    {% if soon.length %}
    <ul class="ap-soon-tiles">
      {% for s in soon %}
      <li>
        <img src="{{ s.logo }}" alt="" width="44" height="44" loading="lazy">
        <div><b>RosterWise&trade; {{ s.name }}</b><span>Coming soon &middot; {{ s.subtext }}</span>
        {% if s.hub %}<a href="{{ s.hub }}">Read the {{ s.name | lower }} guides&nbsp;&rarr;</a>{% endif %}</div>
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
</section>

<!-- From families, and who built it -->
<section class="product-section product-section--cream ap-trust">
  <div class="container">
    {% set reviewed = live | withReviews(appReviews) %}
    {% if reviewed.length %}{% set rs = reviewed[0] %}{% include "app-review.njk" %}{% endif %}
    <h2>Built by a soccer family, for every recruiting family</h2>
    <p>RosterWise started with a question at a tournament, one parent asking another: <em>&ldquo;How do you even figure out where your kid fits?&rdquo;</em> The honest answer was hundreds of roster pages and a spreadsheet. We built the tool we couldn&rsquo;t find, one that reads the rosters themselves. RosterWise is built by Grobe Games LLC.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Everything about a program, in one place (Scott's note on ap-trust, 2026-11-01) -->
<section class="product-section product-section--white ap-depth">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="ap-kicker">In every app</p>
    <h2>Everything about a program, in one place</h2>
    <p class="ap-depth-lead">Open a program and it&rsquo;s all there: the roster by position and class year, the room at your athlete&rsquo;s position, where the players come from, the clubs and high schools that feed the roster, who transferred in and from where, the school&rsquo;s admit rate, test scores and cost, and how long the head coach has been there. The same depth, program after program{% for s in live %}{% set floor = s.slug | teamFloor(previews) %}<span data-ap-for="{{ s.slug }}"{% if not loop.first %} hidden{% endif %}>{% if floor %}, across {{ floor }} college {{ s.name | lower }} teams{% endif %}</span>{% endfor %}, all in one app. What used to take a weekend of roster pages and spreadsheets is a tap away, so your family&rsquo;s time goes to the programs that fit.</p>
    <div class="ap-lists">
      <div>
        <h3>On every roster</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><b>Room at your position:</b> who&rsquo;s listed, who leaves after this season, who&rsquo;s new</li>
          <li><b>Class years</b> and openings by position</li>
          <li><b>Where players come from:</b> states, countries, clubs and high schools</li>
          <li><b>Transfers</b>, matched to the college they left</li>
          <li><b>What changed</b> since the last roster</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>On every school</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><b>Admit rate and test scores</b></li>
          <li><b>Cost</b>, campus size and setting</li>
          <li><b>Conference</b> standings, and the head coach&rsquo;s tenure</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>For your athlete</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><b>My RosterFit&trade;:</b> a fit band, with a light for each factor</li>
          <li><b>Compare</b> programs side by side, and save favorites with notes</li>
          <li><b>A recruiting timeline</b> that opens at your athlete&rsquo;s year</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="ap-limits">RosterWise reports what the rosters show. It doesn&rsquo;t rank programs or predict recruiting outcomes. <a href="/roster-intelligence/">How roster intelligence works&nbsp;&rarr;</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- FAQ -->
<section class="product-section product-section--cream">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 style="text-align: center;">Questions families ask</h2>
    <div class="faq-list">
      {% for item in faq %}
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>{{ item.q }}</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <p>{{ item.a | safe }}</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Final call to action, for the chosen sport -->
<section class="product-final-cta">
  <div class="inner">
    <h2>Ready to find your athlete&rsquo;s fit?</h2>
    <p>{{ live | pluck("name") | andList }} {{ "are" if live.length > 1 else "is" }} available now, each in its own app. Free to try; $39.99 once for full access.</p>
    {% for s in live %}
    <p class="ap-final-cta" data-ap-for="{{ s.slug }}"{% if not loop.first %} hidden{% endif %}>
      <a class="ap-btn ap-btn--gold" href="{{ s.appStoreUrl }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Get RosterWise {{ s.name }} free</a>
    </p>
    {% endfor %}
    <p class="ap-explore">
      {% for s in apps.sports %}{% if s.hub %}<a href="{{ s.hub }}">Explore {{ s.name }}&nbsp;&rarr;</a>{% endif %}{% endfor %}
      <a href="/guide/">Recruiting guides&nbsp;&rarr;</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<script src="/assets/app-page.js?v=2" defer></script>
